## C. Asymmetric intervals (skew-normal errors, zero mean, unit sd)

An interval [p-a, p+b] is the symmetric interval about its midpoint p+(b-a)/2, so
'asymmetric about the prediction' == 'symmetric about a shifted centre'.  The
question is only how much a FREE midpoint beats a midpoint fixed at mean/median.

| shape a | skewness | k | R* midpoint=mean | R* midpoint=median | R* free (HDI) | gain vs median |
